#### Asynchronous JSONL Streaming
An asynchronous SDK client is also available for JSONL streaming. It returns a [`CompletableFuture`][comp-fut] that completes with the same blocking `JsonLStream<T>` iterator once the stream is connected. See [Asynchronous Support](#asynchronous-support) for more details.
{{templateUsageSection "jsonl" "" nil nil nil true}}

[jsonl-format]: https://jsonlines.org/
[x-ndjson]: https://github.com/ndjson/ndjson-spec
[comp-fut]: https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/util/concurrent/CompletableFuture.html
  {{- else}}
#### Reactive Streams Interoperability
An asynchronous SDK client is also available for JSONL streaming that returns a [`Flow.Publisher<T>`][flow-pub]. See [Asynchronous Support](#asynchronous-support) for more details on async benefits and reactive library integration.
{{templateUsageSection "jsonl" "" nil nil nil true}}

[jsonl-format]: https://jsonlines.org/
[x-ndjson]: https://github.com/ndjson/ndjson-spec
[flow-pub]: https://docs.oracle.com/javase/9/docs/api/java/util/concurrent/Flow.Publisher.html
  {{- end}}
{{- end}}